Package: transDIF
Title: Score Comparability for Translated and Adapted Exams
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daniel", "Edi", email = "danieledi2026@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5475-819X"))
Description: An adaptation-comparability workflow for small, lower-scoring
    and unbalanced language groups where standard DIF tools break down.
    Calibrates the Rasch model in each language group, models between-language
    difficulty differences with an empirical-Bayes spike-and-slab mixture
    that jointly performs robust linking, anchor selection and small-sample
    DIF detection with local false discovery rate control, quantifies whether
    item-level DIF accumulates into different pass rates, explains DIF by
    item features to give translators actionable guidance, and drafts a
    comparability report.
